1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,030
Hi!

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:05,780
- Hey! - Hi!

3
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:09,240
- How was the honeymoon? - Oh, incredible!

4
00:00:10,564 --> 00:00:14,640
Champagne, candle-lit dinners, moonlight walks on the beach.

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,820
It was so romantic.

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,740
- Where's Mike? - He's at the doctor.

7
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,400
He didn't poop while we were there.

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,280
I'm glad you're back. I need your help.

9
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,320
Oh, why, what's up?

10
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,300
I have an audition for this play, and I have to speak French which, according to my resume,

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,300
I'm fluent in.

12
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:35,720
Joey, you shouldn't lie on your resume.

13
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:37,560
Yeah, you really shouldn't.

14
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:40,320
By the way, how was that yearlong dig in Cairo?

15
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:43,340
It was okay.

16
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,300
I did not know you spoke French.

17
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:52,920
You're so sexy.

18
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:55,200
Well, so will you help me?

19
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,100
I really wanna be in this play.

20
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:57,000
Sure.

21
00:00:59,728 --> 00:01:00,858
Seriously, stop it.

22
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:01,740
I'm gonna jump on you.

23
00:01:03,774 --> 00:01:05,914
《老友记》第十季第十三集 乔伊说法语

24
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:45,460
- Hey. - Hi.

25
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:46,660
Why are you wearing my apron?

26
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,120
I'm making cookies for Erica.

27
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,640
We have to leave soon.

28
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,320
Her plane comes in in about an hour.

29
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:59,180
When she gets here, is it okay if I introduce you two as my wife and the woman who's carrying my child?

30
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,000
No?

31
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:03,720
Divorce?

32
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,300
- Hey. - Hey.

33
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,280
You know where Rachel is?

34
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,660
No, we haven't haven't seen her since morning.

35
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,340
It's unbelievable.

36
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,880
She was supposed to meet me a half-hour ago with Emma.

37
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:15,740
- Hey! - Hey!

38
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,180
These are for Erica!

39
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,960
She's gonna eat all those cookies?

40
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:22,340
Well, I want the baby to come out all cute and fat!

41
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:26,860
So why is Erica coming to visit?

42
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,480
We wanna get to know her better.

43
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:31,460
And she's never been to New York, so she wants to see the tourist spots:

44
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:33,800
Statue of Liberty, Empire State Building.

45
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:38,020
Oh, those places! There's always so many people, and they're being corralled like cattle.

46
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,840
And, you know, there's always some idiot who goes, "Moo."

47
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,760
Well, if it annoys you so much, then why do you do it?

48
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:50,680
Oh, hi. Hi. Thanks for showing up

49
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:51,660
30 minutes late.

50
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:52,160
Ross.

51
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,180
No, I'm sure you have a great excuse.

52
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,660
What was it, a hair appointment?

53
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,040
A mani-pedi?

54
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,900
Barneys:纽约时尚精品店

55
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,480
Was there a sale at Barneys?

56
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,520
My father had a heart attack.

57
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:03,600
While I was at Barneys.

58
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,120
- Oh, my God, Rach. - Honey?

59
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:11,600
- I'm so sorry. - Is he okay?

60
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:14,540
Yeah, he's gonna be fine, but he's heavily sedated.

61
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:16,740
Okay, I'm gonna go to Long lsland with you.

62
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,340
I mean, you can't be alone right now.

63
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,280
No, come on, I'm totally okay.

64
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:23,060
I don't need you to come.

65
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:26,060
I can totally handle this on my own.

66
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,920
Still, still, let me come for me.

67
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,480
Okay. If you really need to.

68
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:36,300
I bet someone could use one of Monica's freshly baked cookies.

69
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:37,760
Oh, I really could.

70
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,140
All right, it seems pretty simple.

71
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,700
Your first line is, "My name is Claude."

72
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,600
So just repeat after me.

73
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,700
- Well, let's try it again. - Okay.

74
00:04:10,264 --> 00:04:13,620
It's not quite what I'm saying.

75
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:17,820
Really? Sounds exactly the same to me.

76
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:20,060
- It does, really? - Yeah.

77
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:22,820
- Let's just try it again. - Okay.

78
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,380
- Really listen. - Got it.

79
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:39,280
- Hey, you guys! - Hi.

80
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,540
I want you to meet someone really special.

81
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:44,860
Phoebe, this is Erica. And this is the baby!

82
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:48,240
- Joey, Erica, baby. - Hi.

83
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,880
Everyone, Erica! Baby!

84
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:53,700
Monica. Calm. Self.

85
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,420
- Hey, sit down. - Thank you.

86
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,120
It's really nice to meet you guys.

87
00:04:58,220 --> 00:04:59,340
I can't believe I'm here.

88
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,900
Well, welcome to New York City, or should I say:

89
00:05:01,993 --> 00:05:03,783
不知所云的法语

90
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,680
Why would you say that?

91
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:11,300
Okay. What are you gonna be doing today?

92
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:13,180
Well, I wanna see everything!

93
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:16,420
Times Square, Coney lsland, Rockefeller Center.

94
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,440
Oh, you know what you should do?

95
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:19,860
You should walk to the top of the Statue of Liberty.

96
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:22,040
- Oh, yeah, let's do that. - Great.

97
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,660
This baby better be really good.

98
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:32,360
Hi. Excuse me,

99
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,220
I'm here to see my father.

100
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,220
My name is Rachel Green.

101
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,380
And I'm Dr. Ross Geller.

102
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:37,520
Ross, please, this is a hospital.

103
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:39,810
Doctor:医生也是博士的意思

104
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:39,500
That actually means something here.

105
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,480
- So can we please go in? - Absolutely.

106
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:47,340
Rach, I think I'm gonna wait out here because my throat is feeling a little scratchy.

107
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:48,640
I don't wanna infect him.

108
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,840
Ross, please. Don't be so scared of him.

109
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:53,300
I am not scared of him. I'm really sick.

110
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,360
He's under sedation, so he's pretty much out.

111
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,200
I'm feeling better.

112
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:01,600
Oh, my God.

113
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:08,960
That ear and nose hair trimmer I got him was just money down the drain, huh?

114
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:10,960
Ms. Green?

115
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:13,960
Your father's doctor's on the phone if you'd like to speak to him.

116
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,760
Oh, great. Are you gonna be okay?

117
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,760
He's unconscious. We'll be just fine.

118
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:18,760
Okay.

119
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:59,040
- Did the TV wake you? - No.

120
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:03,320
When you put your feet up on my bed, you tugged on my catheter.

121
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:12,280
What are you doing here, Geller?

122
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:15,480
Well, I came with Rachel, who should be back any second.

123
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,640
So, what's new?

124
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,040
Oh, I had a little heart attack.

125
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,700
Right. Is it painful?

126
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:25,400
What, the heart attack or sitting here talking to you?

127
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,240
Let's see if we can get that Rachel back in here.

128
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:31,940
So, what's new with you?

129
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:34,420
Knocked up any more of my daughters lately?

130
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,160
Nope. Just the one. Rach!

131
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:44,220
No!

132
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,620
Okay, maybe if we just break it down.

133
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:51,260
Okay, let's try it one syllable at a time.

134
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:53,220
Okay, so repeat after me.

135
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,840
Great! Okay, faster.

136
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,180
Okay, it's too hard. I can't teach you.

137
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:09,860
What are you doing?

138
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:12,260
I have to go before I put your head through a wall.

139
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,760
Don't go, I need you!

140
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,380
My audition is tomorrow!

141
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:39,000
Hey. I was gonna make us some dinner but all I found in your dad's fridge was bacon and heavy cream.

142
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:42,400
I think we solved the mystery of the heart attack.

143
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:44,660
Did you call your parents?

144
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,060
Oh, yeah. Emma's doing great.

145
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:46,720
Oh, good.

146
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:54,280
- What? - I just can't believe I'm in Rachel Green's room.

147
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:56,480
What do you mean?

148
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,620
You've been in my room before.

149
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,600
Yeah, sure, right.

150
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,320
Like I'd ever be in Rachel Green's room.

151
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,200
Okay, I gotta tell you, it's really weird when you use my whole name.

152
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:08,520
Sorry.

153
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,200
- You okay? - Yeah.

154
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,680
- Yeah, you had a rough day. - Yeah.

155
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:17,820
It's just so weird seeing him like that, you know?

156
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:18,820
I mean, he's a doctor.

157
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,580
You don't expect doctors to get sick.

158
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:23,560
But we do.

159
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,100
He's gonna be okay, Rach.

160
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:36,700
I don't want him to wake up alone.

161
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:37,640
I should go to the hospital.

162
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,820
What? No, no. Hey, hey, look.

163
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:40,160
What?

164
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,800
They gave him a lot of medication.

165
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,820
He wouldn't even know if you were there.

166
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,280
We'll go see him first thing in the morning. Ok?

167
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:47,940
Really? I shouldn't feel guilty?

168
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,160
No-- God, hey.

169
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,480
Rach, you've been an amazing daughter, okay?

170
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,000
Right now you need to get some rest.

171
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:54,540
Okay, maybe you're right.

172
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:56,600
Good night.

173
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:00,380
Wait, wait, wait.

174
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,700
Would you stay here with me for a little while?

175
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,260
- Sure. - Okay.

176
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:11,620
Thank you for coming with me today.

177
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,740
Oh, of course.

178
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,700
Rachel Green is very happy you're in her room.

179
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:19,480
Me too. Come here.

180
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,660
I just don't wanna be alone tonight.

181
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:25,920
Okay, well,

182
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:30,040
I can maybe grab a sleeping bag or--

183
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:45,960
No, Rach!

184
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:48,500
I'm sorry,

185
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:51,320
I just don't think this is a good idea.

186
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:53,340
Well, we won't know that until we do it,

187
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:54,890
will we?

188
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:55,960
No, look, uh.

189
00:10:57,200 --> 00:11:03,880
You are upset about your father, and you're feeling vulnerable and I just don't feel it would be right.

190
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:06,560
I feel like I'd be, you know, taking advantage of you.

191
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:07,780
What--? Taking advantage?

192
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,220
I am giving you the advantage. Enjoy!

193
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:17,880
Look, I'm sure it would be great but I think one of us has to be thinking clearly.

194
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,180
So I'm gonna go.

195
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:27,430
Okay.

196
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:31,820
I'll see you in the morning.

197
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:37,420
I haven't had sex in four months.

198
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,940
I should get a medal for that!

199
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,340
Thanks so much for taking me to all those places.

200
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,260
I had a great time.

201
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:50,280
I'm glad.

202
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,220
Listen, I wanna apologize about Chandler, though.

203
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,720
I just did not see this coming.

204
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:56,160
New York is awesome!

205
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,080
What is with you?

206
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:03,440
You know, I've been to these places before but I've never really seen them.

207
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:05,440
Yeah, you miss a lot when you're mooing.

208
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:09,900
Thank you for showing me around.

209
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,380
Oh, it was our pleasure.

210
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,640
We're so much enjoying getting to know you.

211
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:16,280
Well, if there's anything else you wanna know....

212
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:19,860
Okay.

213
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:23,920
Can we ask you some questions about the father?

214
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,900
Oh, sure. Yeah.

215
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:31,300
Well, he was my high-school boyfriend, captain of the football team, really cute.

216
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:33,960
Got a scholarship and went to college.

217
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:34,980
That's great.

218
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:39,440
Yeah, it's almost definitely him.

219
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:42,440
How's that, now?

220
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,780
Well, there's a chance it's another guy.

221
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:51,900
I mean, I've only ever been with two guys but they sort of overlapped.

222
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,620
So, what does the other guy do?

223
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,160
Does he go to college too?

224
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,500
No, he's in prison.

225
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,200
Was he falsely accused of something?

226
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:05,600
No.

227
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,320
He killed his father with a shovel.

228
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,420
Other than that, he's a great guy.

229
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,860
I'll bet his dad doesn't think so.

230
00:13:24,768 --> 00:13:27,028
- Are you awake? - Of course I'm awake.

231
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:28,860
Assume from now on that I'm always awake.

232
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:33,800
All right, we don't know that it's him.

233
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,240
I mean, it could be the football guy.

234
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,300
Honey, it's us.

235
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:37,920
Of course it's the shovel killer.

236
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:45,000
Well, all right, let's say that it is him.

237
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,800
Would we not want the baby? No.

238
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,380
Would we treat him any differently?

239
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,800
I'd keep an eye on him.

240
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:55,200
We have to find out who the father is.

241
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:57,140
- How? - I don't know.

242
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:58,940
They have tests for these things, right?

243
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,200
Yes, but maybe we're just overreacting.

244
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:02,580
Easy for you to say.

245
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:03,900
He's a father killer.

246
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:07,380
He probably loves his mommy.

247
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:10,760
He's probably got a tattoo that says "Mom" on his shovel-wielding arm.

248
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:18,440
<i>We'll now count from one to five.</i>

249
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:31,500
- <i>Good job.</i> - Thank you.

250
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:34,780
- Hey. - Hey, Joey.

251
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:39,740
Listen, I feel really badly about yesterday, and I thought about it a lot.

252
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,380
No, I was too impatient.

253
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,980
So let's try it again.

254
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,200
That's okay. I don't need your help.

255
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,700
I worked on it myself, and I gotta say I am pretty good.

256
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,640
Really, can I hear some of it?

257
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:51,760
Sure, sure.

258
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:54,540
Okay.

259
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:04,130
See?

260
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:06,400
You, you're not--

261
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:08,640
You're not-- You're--

